        (*parser.Part)({
          Name: (string) "",
          Type: (string) (len=9) "paragraph",
          Value: (string) (len=647) "His life and legacy of scientific and political achievement, and his status as one of America's most influential Founding Fathers, have seen Franklin honored for more than two centuries after his death on the $100 bill and in the names of warships, many towns and counties, educational institutions and corporations, as well as in numerous cultural references and a portrait in the Oval Office. His more than 30,000 letters and documents have been collected in The Papers of Benjamin Franklin. Anne Robert Jacques Turgot said of him: \"Eripuit fulmen cœlo, mox sceptra tyrannis\" (\"He snatched lightning from the sky and the scepter from tyrants\").",
