        (*parser.Part)({
          Name: (string) "",
          Type: (string) (len=9) "paragraph",
          Value: (string) (len=620) "Like the other advocates of republicanism, Franklin emphasized that the new republic could survive only if the people were virtuous. All his life, he explored the role of civic and personal virtue, as expressed in Poor Richard's aphorisms. He felt that organized religion was necessary to keep men good to their fellow men, but rarely attended religious services himself. When he met Voltaire in Paris and asked his fellow member of the Enlightenment vanguard to bless his grandson, Voltaire said in English, \"God and Liberty,\" and added, \"this is the only appropriate benediction for the grandson of Monsieur Franklin.\"",
